{"id":"NCT07442071","title":"Impact of Low Dose Epinephrine in the Management of Out-of-hospital Cardiac Arrest on Neurological Outcome","official":"Impact of Low Dose Epinephrine in the Management of Out-of-hospital Cardiac Arrest on Neurological Outcome: A Multicenter Randomized and Double-blind Trial.","summary":"This study will test whether a lower dose of epinephrine (0.5 mg) given during emergency treatment for out-of-hospital cardiac arrest helps more patients survive with good brain function, compared to the standard dose (1 mg). Adults who experience cardiac arrest outside the hospital and are treated by emergency medical teams will be randomly assigned to receive either the low dose or the standard dose of epinephrine. The study will compare survival and neurological outcomes between the two groups over 28 days.","conditions":["Out-of-hospital Cardiac Arrest (OHCA)"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Epinephrine 0.5 mg intravenous bolus"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Epinephrine 1 mg intravenous bolus"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\nMale or female, aged ≥18 years. Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest for which resuscitation is decided by the SMUR team.\n\nMedical Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest. Affiliated with or beneficiary of a social security plan\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Non-medical Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (traumatic, drownings, electrocution, asphyxia, overdose, unknown cause).\n* Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest without advanced life support (Do Not Attempt Resuscitation order, body finding, the decision not to attempt advanced life support is at the physician's discretion).\n\n  * Pregnant women, birthing or breastfeeding mothers\n  * Adults under legal protection measure (such as guardianship, conservatorship)\n  * Individuals deprived of liberty due to judicial or administrative decision","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":4336,"start":"2026-06","pcd":"2030-07","upd":"2026-03-02","sponsor":"Central Hospital, Nancy, France","areas":["other"],"central":["Tahar CHOUIHED, MD, PhD · 0033383157322 · T.CHOUIHEDMAHJOUB@chru-nancy.fr","Nicolas Girerd, MD PhD · 0033383157322 · n.girerd@chru-nancy.fr"],"sites":[{"f":"CH Annecy","city":"Annecy","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":45.9088,"lon":6.1257,"c":"Hugo SCHMIT, MD PHD · +33 4 50 63 63 63 · hschmit@ch-annecygenevois.fr"},{"f":"Centre hospitalier de la Côte Basque","city":"Bayonne","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":43.4932,"lon":-1.473,"c":"Pereira Xavier, MD · +33 5 59 44 35 35 · xpereira@ch-cotebasque.fr"},{"f":"CHU Besancon","city":"Besançon","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":47.2488,"lon":6.0182,"c":"Abdo KHOURY, MD · 0033381668836 · akhoury@chu-besancon.fr"},{"f":"CHU Brest","city":"Brest","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":48.3903,"lon":-4.4863,"c":"Adrien Basset, MD · +33 2 98 22 33 33 · adrien.basset@chu-brest.fr"},{"f":"CHU Colmar","city":"Colmar","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":48.0808,"lon":7.3558,"c":"Yannick GOTTWALLES, MD · +33 3 89 12 40 00 · yannick.GOTTWALLES@ch-colmar.fr"},{"f":"CH SUD Francilien","city":"Corbeil-Essonnes","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":48.606,"lon":2.4876,"c":"Romain BARDELAY, MD · 0033161696169 · secretariat@samu91.org"},{"f":"Brigade de Sapeurs-Pompiers de Paris","city":"Courbevoie","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":48.8967,"lon":2.2567,"c":"Simon-Pierre CORCOSTEGUI, MD · 0033149047425 · simon-pierre.corcostegui@pompiersparis.fr"},{"f":"Centre Hospitalier Universitaire Grenoble Alpes","city":"La Tronche","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":45.2051,"lon":5.7463,"c":"Nicolas SEGOND, MD · 0033476767575 · nsegond@chu.grenoble.fr"},{"f":"Hospices Civils De Lyon","city":"Lyon","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":45.7491,"lon":4.8479,"c":""},{"f":"CHU Montpellier","city":"Montpellier","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":43.6109,"lon":3.8763,"c":"Thomas SANCHEZ, MD · +33 4 67 33 67 33 · thomas-sanchez@chu-montpellier.fr"},{"f":"CHRU Nancy","city":"Nancy"